  "description": "STARTER list of well-known package names, used by the optional package install check (offline mode). It is NOT the registry and it is NOT exhaustive: a name missing from this list is never reported, and a name on it is never reported either. It only gives the check something to compare an unfamiliar name with.",
  "created": "2026-11-05",
  "how_it_was_made": "Every name was checked against its registry (npm: time.created; PyPI: earliest upload) with `node .github/scripts/check-package-names.mjs --min-days 365 --add pypi:motor --add pypi:authlib --add pypi:parse --write` on 2026-11-05 (UTC). Kept only names that exist and whose first release is at least 365 days old. Checked 747, dropped 1 (missing 0, too young 0, no answer after one retry 1).",
  "regenerate": "Replace it from the registries' own download rankings, keep only names a maintainer has confirmed, lowercase npm names, write PyPI names with the registry's own normalisation (lowercase, runs of - _ . replaced by one -), keep the two lists sorted, and update 'created'. A few hundred names per registry is enough: the check only compares near spellings.",
